======================================================================
GROUP D: M2 = 1-m1-m2 deterministic given (m1,m2); prob(D|m1,m2)=1-m1-m2
Step-A density of (m1,m2) is 2 on T={m1,m2>0,m1+m2<1}.
======================================================================
weighted marginal density of L=m1+m2 (group D mass at each ell): 2*ell*(1 - ell)
=> f_D(x) = 2*x*(1 - x)
total probability mass of Group D (sanity, direct): 1/3
total probability mass of Group D (direct double integral): 1/3

======================================================================
GROUP B: M2 = 1-m2-D1, D1~U(0,m1); prob(B|m1,m2)=m1(1-m2)
======================================================================
joint density of (m1,m2,d1) restricted to group B (indep of d1!) = 2 - 2*m2  on {0<d1<m1, (m1,m2) in T}
=> f_B(x) = -x**3 + x

======================================================================
GROUP C: M2 = 1-m1-D2, D2~U(0,m2); prob(C|m1,m2)=m2(1-m1)  [mirror of B]
======================================================================
=> f_C(x) = -x**3 + x

======================================================================
GROUP A: M2 = 1-D1-D2, D1~U(0,m1),D2~U(0,m2) indep; prob(A|m1,m2)=2 m1 m2
======================================================================
joint density of (m1,m2,d1,d2) restricted to group A = 4  (constant) on {0<d1<m1,0<d2<m2,(m1,m2) in T}
marginal joint density of (D1,D2)=(d1,d2) within group A = 2*(d1 + d2 - 1)**2  on {d1,d2>0, d1+d2<1}
marginal density of sigma=D1+D2 within group A, f_sigma(sigma) = 2*sigma*(sigma - 1)**2
=> f_A(x) = 2*x**2*(1 - x)

======================================================================
SUMMING ALL FOUR GROUPS
======================================================================
f_A(x) = 2*x**2*(1 - x)
f_B(x) = -x**3 + x
f_C(x) = -x**3 + x
f_D(x) = 2*x*(1 - x)

f_{M2}(x) = f_A+f_B+f_C+f_D = 4*x*(1 - x**2)
Target 4x(1-x^2) = -4*x**3 + 4*x
Symbolic difference f_M2 - target = 0
EXACT MATCH: True

